# Local agent/cache metadata
.agents/
.codex/
.claude/

# Raw and derived data
Input/
data_intermediate/
data_processed/

# Generated outputs, scratch work, and historical output bundles
Output/*
# AUD-1 audit outputs: PACK-1 consumes these as its direct input, so they need version
# history. Git cannot re-include a path inside an excluded DIRECTORY, so the rule above is
# 'Output/*' (contents) rather than 'Output/' (the directory itself). Nothing else is tracked.
!Output/audit/
# PACK-1: the item list and manifests are the record of what shipped and to which
# checksum, so they need version history. The copied artefacts under Output/pack/
# subfolders stay ignored. Four lines, not two: 'Output/*' excludes the pack DIRECTORY,
# so it must be re-included before anything inside it can be.
!Output/pack/
Output/pack/*
!Output/pack/*.csv
!Output/pack/*.md
# DIAG-1 / SPAT-1 (Ruling BB, 7 Aug 2026): the assumptions record is tracked for
# CITABILITY, not rebuildability. METHODS-REG cites this document, and a methods
# appendix citing an artefact absent from the repository is the one-sided citation
# XCHECK-1 flagged, made structural. The PANELS stay ignored - they are re-rendered
# from the tracked tables. Same four-line shape as the pack rules above, and the
# 'analysis/' subfolder needs its own pair because 'Output/diag/*' excludes the
# DIRECTORY: those three boundary CSVs are the bytes every result row's checksum
# refers to, so a citation cannot be verified without them.
!Output/diag/
Output/diag/*
!Output/diag/*.csv
!Output/diag/*.md
!Output/diag/*.txt
!Output/diag/analysis/
Output/diag/analysis/*
!Output/diag/analysis/*.csv
# GLM-1, same rationale and same four-line shape (Ruling BB): the findings, the
# pre-registration and the comparison tables are tracked for citability; the envelope
# plots are re-rendered from them.
!Output/glm/
Output/glm/*
!Output/glm/*.csv
!Output/glm/*.md
# Ruling CL (8 Aug 2026): EXEMPLAR1_units.csv only, on the same citability grounds as
# Output/diag/* under Ruling BB - it carries the nine units' support level, scope filter,
# pixel constant, denominator and period label, and the report cites it. Output/tables is
# NOT un-ignored wholesale; this is one targeted path.
!Output/tables/
Output/tables/*
!Output/tables/EXEMPLAR1_units.csv
working/
/archive/
_local_archive/
docs/archive/
# C9 (Tier2H): un-ignore docs/archive so the superseded Task F design docs are
# tracked — a gitignored archive is not memory. Keep other archive contents ignored.
!docs/archive/
docs/archive/*
!docs/archive/Tier1_TaskF_spatial_resampling_spec_v2.md
!docs/archive/Gayini_subsampling_approach.md
# Task U: same C9 reasoning. v1 and v1.1 are the provenance chain for the Gate U0
# findings that superseded them, and record the withdrawn preview figures where a
# reader can recognise them rather than re-quote them.
!docs/archive/LiDAR/
!docs/archive/LiDAR/*.md
R/obs/

# Script history is now tracked through docs/scripts_manifest.csv
# and scripts/archive/ manifests. Do not add a new scripts/obs/
# compatibility folder; archive legacy scripts under scripts/archive/.

